# state: first-run   (recorded on a disk with no save for the title (NOTES.md E); lane.savestate433)
# Grand Theft Auto III (5454000E): one route for the first run (no save on
# the disk, so START at the title begins a new game; the game saves only
# at a safehouse, so every first-run attempt boots the same way).
# PATHFOUND by pathfind.py on the Nova, 2026-10-11 (lane.gtaroutes1011
# session 1034707; path recorded to pathknow/paths/5454000E.json, gameplay
# reached in 2.2 min / 14 steps).
#
#   Loading icon -> several Rockstar/publisher-logo screens and a black
#   frame (~50 s, non-interactive) -> intro credits video (A skips it) ->
#   title screen "Press START" (START) -> betrayal/bridge-explosion
#   cutscene (A skips it) -> second cutscene (A skips it) -> Portland
#   street, Claude on foot, full HUD (health, money, radar, wanted level).
#
# The intro-video and cutscene skips are trains of A presses 5 s apart (as
# gta-sa.route): loading time differs between runs, and an A that lands on
# a loading/logo screen is a no-op. Player control: pathfind's probe step
# moved the player with LY up. The play pattern runs, sprints, steers and
# turns the camera; it never presses Y, START or BACK after the title.
#
